		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Honey that Dynamax Vespiquen produces.\nAdding this honey to Max Soup makes the\ntaste very smooth.\rIt also has the same effect as a Max Revive.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01599" index="1599">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Mushrooms that have the power of\nchanging Dynamax forms. They boost\nall stats of a Pokémon during battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01600" index="1600">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A twig from a species of tree called\nGalarica that grows in certain areas\naround the Galar region.\rIt’s a material for an accessory for a\ncertain Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01601" index="1601">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Having one of these cards increases\nthe selection available to you in\nboutiques and hair salons.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01602" index="1602">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A pass to go to the Isle of Armor.\nShow it to the rail staff at\nWedgehurst Station.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01603" index="1603">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This bike can do a turbo boost\nand run on the water using\nRotom’s power.\rIt’s a sparkling white that\nshines brilliantly.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01604" index="1604">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This bike can do a turbo boost\nand run on the water using\nRotom’s power.\rIt’s a glistening black\nthat shines reddish-black.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01605" index="1605">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Having one of these charms increases\nthe Exp. Points your Pokémon get. It’s a\nstretchy charm that encourages growth.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01606" index="1606">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Rare ore that can be obtained on the Isle\nof Armor. Something good will happen if you\ngive it to a collector on the Isle of Armor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01607" index="1607">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Having one of these mysterious and unique\ncharms makes it more likely you’ll encounter\na Pokémon with a mark.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01608" index="1608">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Reins that people presented to the king.\nThey enhance Calyrex’s power over bountiful\nharvests and unite Calyrex with its steed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01609" index="1609">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Reins that people presented to the king.\nThey enable those who are connected to\ncommunicate with each other.\rThe reins separate Calyrex and its\nbeloved steed.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01610" index="1610">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A clue about the King of Bountiful Harvests.\nIt’s written by Peony, and an old photo\nis attached to it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01611" index="1611">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A clue about the legend of giants.\nIt’s written by Peony and has unique\ndrawings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01612" index="1612">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A clue about the legend of bird Pokémon.\nIt’s written by Peony and has a unique\ndrawing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01613" index="1613">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A mysterious clue that\nPeony seems to have\ndropped.\rThere’s a photo attached\nto it showing a shining hole\nopening above the Max Lair.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01614" index="1614">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A pass to go to the Crown Tundra.\nShow it to the rail staff at\nWedgehurst Station.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01615" index="1615">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A mysterious object made of wood.\nPart of it seems to be chipped.\nMaybe it’s meant to be part of something.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01616" index="1616">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A single petal that the King of\nBountiful Harvests gave you.\nIt radiates faint light.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01617" index="1617">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Mane hair that belonged to the King of\nBountiful Harvests’ steed, Glastrier.\nThe hair is strong and very flexible.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01618" index="1618">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Mane hair that belonged to the King of\nBountiful Harvests’ steed, Spectrier.\nThe hair is very smooth to the touch.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01619" index="1619">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Produce that the King of Bountiful\nHarvests’ beloved steed likes to eat.\nIt grew in a field covered in snow.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01620" index="1620">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Produce that the King of Bountiful\nHarvests’ beloved steed likes to eat.\nIt grew in a gloomy field.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01621" index="1621">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Mysterious ore that can\nbe obtained in the\nMax Lair.\rSomething good will happen if you give\nit to a collector in the Crown Tundra.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01622" index="1622">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Seeds to plant in a field. The kind of\ncarrot you’ll get is determined by\nwhich field you plant the seeds in.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01623" index="1623">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A patch that can be used to change\nthe regular Ability of a Pokémon\nto a rarer Ability.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01624" index="1624">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Cords that shine when you hold them\nup to the light. The people of old\ntimes presented these to the King of\rBountiful Harvests to express their\ngratitude.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01625" index="1625">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A mysterious balm that somehow has\nthe power to calm Dialga in its\nfrenzy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01626" index="1626">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A mysterious balm that somehow has\nthe power to calm Palkia in its\nfrenzy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01627" index="1627">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A mysterious balm to be used when\nbattling Arceus.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01628" index="1628">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A baked treat made from Berries\nand other ingredients, which is often\neaten in regions such as Galar.\rIt is beloved by a surprising number of\nPokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01629" index="1629">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A fruit whose shell can be used to form\nthe capsules of all manner of Poké Balls\nwhen crafting them from scratch.\rIts proper name is actually “Brown\nApricorn.”</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01630" index="1630">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A hidden gem gaining popularity\nin Jubilife Village and beloved\nby Pokémon.\rThis sweet treat can be fed\nto a Pokémon to cure any status\ncondition it may have.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01631" index="1631">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An item that sharply boosts the\noffensive and defensive stats\nof a Pokémon in battle.\rThese effects disappear if\nthe Pokémon leaves the battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01632" index="1632">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An item that sharply boosts the\ncritical-hit ratio of a Pokémon\nin battle.\rThis effect disappears if the Pokémon\nleaves the battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01633" index="1633">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A dumpling that will make\na Pokémon become fixated\non a move in battle.\rThe Pokémon will deal more damage when\nusing that move but will take more damage\nas well.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01634" index="1634">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">These pickled vegetables\nprime a Pokémon for\nbattle.\rThe Pokémon takes a hard-hitting stance,\nwhich boosts the damage dealt by its moves\nby 50 percent.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01635" index="1635">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When eaten, this curious snack temporarily\nswaps a Pokémon’s offensive stats with\nits defensive stats.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01636" index="1636">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A fern used for crafting items to be thrown.\nWhen these curled leaves are unfurled,\nthey can serve as nature’s wrapping paper.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01637" index="1637">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A rare seed that can be given to the\ncaptain of the Security Corps to have\na Pokémon master a move so it can be\rused in the agile style or strong style.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01638" index="1638">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">- - -</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01639" index="1639">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">- - -</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01640" index="1640">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Ice beloved by the Lord of the Tundra,\nAvalugg. This ice is said to be fragments\nof ancient Avalugg that lived long ago.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01641" index="1641">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Proof that you have completed the trial\nset by Uxie, the Being of Knowledge\nthat lives in Lake Acuity.\rThis item is needed to forge the\nRed Chain.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01642" index="1642">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Proof that you have completed the trial\nset by Azelf, the Being of Willpower\nthat lives in Lake Acuity.\rThis item is needed to forge the\nRed Chain.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01643" index="1643">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Proof that you have completed the trial\nset by Mesprit, the Being of Emotion\nthat lives in Lake Acuity.\rThis item is needed to forge the\nRed Chain.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01644" index="1644">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When combined with an Apricorn, this\nmysterious tumbled stone can draw out the\nproperties required to forge a Poké Ball.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01645" index="1645">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A flute that can be used to call\nspecial Pokémon that are willing\nto bear you around the region.\rIts timbre is eerie and mysterious.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01646" index="1646">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An herbal medicine that can\nrestore 60 HP to a Pokémon,\njust as a Potion does.\rYet the bitter taste will make the\nPokémon less friendly toward you.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01647" index="1647">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An herbal medicine that can\nrestore 100 HP to a Pokémon,\njust as a Super Potion does.\rYet the bitter taste will make the\nPokémon less friendly toward you.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01648" index="1648">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Honey that sparkles with an amber hue.\nIt is beloved by bug Pokémon and\nPokémon with fairylike charms,\rso they will gather wherever\na comb of it is thrown.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01649" index="1649">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Beautiful stalks of rice bursting with life.\nPokémon that dwell and wander among the\nfields love these grains and will gather\rwherever the stalks are thrown.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01650" index="1650">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Large, juicy beans that grow in\npods. These beans are beloved by\nfish Pokémon, as well as bird\rPokémon and their flying ilk, so\nthrow one and they will gather\naround.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01651" index="1651">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A large and well-ripened mushroom.\nIt is beloved by the more monstrous\nPokémon, as well as dragon Pokémon,\rso they will gather wherever one is\nthrown.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01652" index="1652">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Translucent crystals that are beloved by\nPokémon bearing a resemblance to grass,\nplants, or minerals.\rThey will gather wherever a lump of this\nsalt is thrown.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01653" index="1653">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A handy log of wood that can be used\nfor anything, from crafting common\ngoods needed for daily living to\rproducing works of art.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01654" index="1654">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The king of herbs, glittering and\nbrilliant. Combining this herb with\nother materials needed to make\rmedicines will boost their efficacy.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01655" index="1655">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A mysterious balm that gives off a soothing\nscent. It can be used to help calm the\nfrenzy of the Lady of the Ridge, Lilligant.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01656" index="1656">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Poké Balls\nfrom scratch. Required materials: 1\nApricorn and 1 Tumblestone.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01657" index="1657">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Great Balls from\nscratch. Required materials: 1 Apricorn,\n1 Iron Chunk, and 1 Tumblestone.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01658" index="1658">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Ultra Balls from\nscratch. Required materials: 1 Apricorn,\n2 Iron Chunks, and 2 Tumblestones.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01659" index="1659">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Feather Balls from\nscratch. Required materials: 1 Apricorn\nand 1 Sky Tumblestone.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01660" index="1660">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Pokéshi Dolls\nfrom scratch.\nRequired materials: 3 logs of Wood.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01661" index="1661">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">- - -</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01662" index="1662">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Smoke Bombs\nfrom scratch. Required materials:\n1 Caster Fern leaf and 1 Sootfoot Root.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01663" index="1663">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Scatter Bangs\nfrom scratch. Required materials: 1\nPop Pod and 1 Caster Fern leaf.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01664" index="1664">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Sticky Globs\nfrom scratch. Required materials: 1\nSpoiled Apricorn, 1 Ball of Mud, and\r1 Caster Fern leaf.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01665" index="1665">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Star Pieces\nfrom scratch. Required materials: 3\nRed Shards, 3 Blue Shards, 3 Green\rShards, and 1 bag of Stardust.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01666" index="1666">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Mushroom Cakes\nfrom scratch. Required materials:\n1 Springy Mushroom and 1 Cake-Lure Base.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01667" index="1667">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A wildflower that can be found\ngrowing across the Hisui region. It\ndoes have medicinal properties, but\rit is so bitter that no wild Pokémon\nwill eat it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01668" index="1668">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Honey Cakes from\nscratch. Required materials: 1 comb of\nDazzling Honey and 1 Cake-Lure Base.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01669" index="1669">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Grain Cakes from\nscratch. Required materials: 1 stalk of\nHearty Grains and 1 Cake-Lure Base.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01670" index="1670">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Bean Cakes from\nscratch. Required materials: 1 pod of\nPlump Beans and 1 Cake-Lure Base.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01671" index="1671">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Salt Cakes from\nscratch. Required materials: 1 hunk of\nCrunchy Salt and 1 Cake-Lure Base.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01672" index="1672">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Potions from scratch.\nRequired materials: 1 Oran Berry and\n1 Medicinal Leek.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01673" index="1673">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Super Potions from\nscratch. Required materials: 1 Potion and\n1 Pep-Up Plant.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01674" index="1674">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Hyper Potions\nfrom scratch. Required materials:\n1 Super Potion and 1 Vivichoke.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01675" index="1675">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Max Potions from\nscratch. Required materials:\n1 Sitrus Berry and 1 bunch of King’s Leaf.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01676" index="1676">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Full Restores\nfrom scratch. Required materials:\n1 Max Potion and 1 Full Heal.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01677" index="1677">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Remedies from\nscratch. Required materials:\n2 Bugwort blooms.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01678" index="1678">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Fine Remedies\nfrom scratch. Required materials: 1\nRemedy and 1 Pep-Up Plant.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01679" index="1679">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Superb Remedies\nfrom scratch. Required materials:\n1 Fine Remedy and 1 Vivichoke.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01680" index="1680">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Old Gateaux from\nscratch.\nRequired materials: 1 pod of Plump Beans,\r1 comb of Dazzling Honey, 1 Sootfoot Root,\nand 1 Cake-Lure Base.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01681" index="1681">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Jubilife Muffins\nfrom scratch. Required materials:\n2 stalks of Hearty Grains, 2 Hopo Berries,\r1 Razz Berry, and 1 Cake-Lure Base.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01682" index="1682">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Full Heals\nfrom scratch. Required materials: 1\nCheri Berry, 1 Pecha Berry, 1 Rawst\rBerry, and 1 Aspear Berry.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01683" index="1683">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Revives from\nscratch. Required materials: 1\nVivichoke and 2 Medicinal Leeks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01684" index="1684">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Max Revives\nfrom scratch. Required materials: 1\nRevive and 2 bunches of King’s Leaf.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01685" index="1685">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Max Ethers\nfrom scratch. Required materials: 1\nLeppa Berry and 2 Pep-Up Plants.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01686" index="1686">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Max Elixirs\nfrom scratch. Required materials: 1\nMax Ether and 2 bunches of King’s\rLeaf.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01687" index="1687">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Stealth Sprays\nfrom scratch. Required materials: 1\nHopo Berry and 3 Bugwort blooms.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01688" index="1688">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">- - -</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01689" index="1689">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Aux Powers\nfrom scratch. Required materials: 2\nbunches of Swordcap and 1 Pep-Up\rPlant.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01690" index="1690">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Aux Guards\nfrom scratch. Required materials: 2\nscraps of Iron Barktongue and 1\rPep-Up Plant.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01691" index="1691">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Dire Hits from\nscratch. Required materials: 2\nDireshrooms and 1 Candy Truffle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01692" index="1692">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Aux Evasions\nfrom scratch. Required materials: 2\nbunches of Doppel Bonnets and 1\rCandy Truffle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01693" index="1693">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Aux\nPowerguards from scratch. Required\nmaterials: 1 Aux Power, 1 Aux Guard,\rand 1 bunch of King’s Leaf.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01694" index="1694">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A mysterious balm that gives off a\nsoothing scent. It can be used to\nhelp calm the frenzy of the Lord of\rthe Woods, Kleavor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01695" index="1695">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A naturally occurring hunk of iron.\nSuch ore is needed to make the\nrequisite parts of numerous Poké\rBall varieties, such as the clasp\nthat holds the ball shut.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01696" index="1696">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">- - -</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01697" index="1697">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When combined with an Apricorn, this\nmysterious black stone can draw out\nthe properties required to forge a\rHeavy Ball.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01698" index="1698">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When combined with an Apricorn, this\nmysterious sky-blue stone can draw\nout the properties required to forge\ra Feather Ball.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01699" index="1699">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">- - -</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01700" index="1700">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A ball of mud that has become stiff\nand hard. Hitting a Pokémon with one\nmay stun the Pokémon, creating an\ropening for you to act.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01701" index="1701">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">- - -</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01702" index="1702">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A sea vegetable used for crafting\nScatter Bangs. If you wrap it up so\nthat the air has no way to escape,\rthen deal it a sharp blow, it\nproduces a loud popping noise.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01703" index="1703">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A tuber used for crafting Smoke\nBombs. It can be mashed for use in\ncooking, but it can also be dried\rand ground to produce a fine powder.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01704" index="1704">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An Apricorn that’s had its insides\neaten. Hitting a Pokémon with one\nmay stun the Pokémon, creating an\ropening for you to act.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01705" index="1705">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A hard ball made of compressed snow.\nHitting a Pokémon with one may stun\nthe Pokémon, creating an opening for\ryou to act.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01706" index="1706">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A ball of some kind of sticky\nsubstance. Hitting a Pokémon with\none may stun the Pokémon, creating\ran opening for you to act.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01707" index="1707">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When used in the field, this spray\nmuffles the sound of your footsteps\nand makes wild Pokémon less likely\rto notice you for a short time.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01708" index="1708">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Required for crafting medicinal\ncompounds. This vegetable is found\ngrowing across the Hisui region and\ris also known as the wayfarer’s\nfriend.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01709" index="1709">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Also called a morning-dew bud. It is\nused as a material for crafting\nitems that can restore vitality to a\rPokémon that has fainted.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01710" index="1710">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Extremely spicy but also highly\nnutritious. This herb is used as a\nmaterial for crafting items that can\rrestore PP to Pokémon or boost their\nstats.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01711" index="1711">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">- - -</language>
	</row>
