	<row id="msg_0221_01757" index="1757">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A fragment that was once\npart of a stone panel in\nthe Solaceon Ruins.\rIt has markings carved on it\nthat appear to be some kind\nof writing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01758" index="1758">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A favored food of Basculegion,\na Pokémon that will bear you\non its back.\rThis food is crafted in an unusual way,\nfrom ingredients gathered via equally\nunusual methods.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01759" index="1759">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A stab-bound journal that once had\npages torn from it. All the pages\nhave been collected and restored.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01760" index="1760">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An improvement on the original\nFeather Ball design. A ball that\nflies fast and true-ideal for\rcatching nimble Pokémon or Pokémon\nthat fly high in the air.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01761" index="1761">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The ultimate iteration of the\nFeather Ball. A ball that flies fast\nand true-ideal for catching nimble\rPokémon or Pokémon that fly high in\nthe air.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01762" index="1762">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A ball that is too heavy to fly high or far,\nbut it is highly effective if you manage\nto hit an unsuspecting Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01763" index="1763">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An improvement on the original Heavy\nBall design. A ball that is too\nheavy to fly high or far, but it is\rhighly effective if you manage to\nhit an unsuspecting Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01764" index="1764">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The ultimate iteration of the Heavy\nBall. A ball that is too heavy to\nfly high or far, but it is highly\reffective if you manage to hit an\nunsuspecting Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01765" index="1765">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Wing Balls from\nscratch. Required materials: 1 Apricorn,\n1 Sky Tumblestone, and 1 Iron Chunk.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01766" index="1766">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Jet Balls from\nscratch. Required materials: 1 Apricorn,\n2 Sky Tumblestones, and 2 Iron Chunks.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01767" index="1767">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A recipe for crafting Heavy Balls from\nscratch. Required materials: 1 Apricorn\nand 1 Black Tumblestone.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01768" index="1768">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Berry that can be fed to a Pokémon\nto restore its PP. If a wild Pokémon\neats one of these Berries, that\rPokémon’s reactions will be dulled.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01769" index="1769">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An herbal medicine that can\nrestore 150 HP to a Pokémon,\njust as a Hyper Potion does.\rYet the bitter taste will make\nthe Pokémon less friendly\ntoward you.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01770" index="1770">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An item that sharply boosts the\noffensive stats of a Pokémon in\nbattle.\rThese effects disappear if the\nPokémon leaves the battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01771" index="1771">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An item that sharply boosts the\ndefensive stats of a Pokémon in\nbattle.\rThese effects disappear if the\nPokémon leaves the battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01772" index="1772">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An item that makes moves less\nlikely to strike a Pokémon in\nbattle.\rThis effect disappears if the\nPokémon leaves the battle.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01773" index="1773">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Mysterious dust that can raise\nthe effort level for one of a\nPokémon’s stats.\rIt can be used to raise\neffort levels only up to\nlevel three, however.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01774" index="1774">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Mysterious gravel that can raise\nthe effort level for one of a\nPokémon’s stats.\rIt can be used only if the effort level\nis at least level three and no greater\nthan level five.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01775" index="1775">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A mysterious pebble that can raise\nthe effort level for one of a\nPokémon’s stats.\rIt can be used only if the effort level\nis at least level six and no greater\nthan level eight.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01776" index="1776">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A mysterious rock that can raise\nthe effort level for one of a\nPokémon’s stats.\rIt can be used only if the effort level\nhas already reached level nine.</language>
	</row>
