		<language name="English">On rare occasions, these shards form\nwhen a Tera Pokémon falls in battle\nand its Tera Jewel shatters.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01889" index="1889">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">On rare occasions, these shards form\nwhen a Tera Pokémon falls in battle\nand its Tera Jewel shatters.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01890" index="1890">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">On rare occasions, these shards form\nwhen a Tera Pokémon falls in battle\nand its Tera Jewel shatters.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01891" index="1891">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An item to be held by Pokémon with select\nAbilities. The energy within this capsule\nboosts the strength of the Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01892" index="1892">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An item to be held by a Pokémon.\nThis cute shield protects the holder\nfrom having its Ability changed by others.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01893" index="1893">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An item to be held by a Pokémon.\nThis amulet protects from stat drops\nfrom opposing moves or abilities.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01894" index="1894">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An item to be held by a Pokémon.\nThis herb allows the holder to mirror an\nopponent’s stat increases--but only once.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01895" index="1895">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An item to be held by a Pokémon.\nThis glove boosts the power of punching\nmoves and prevents direct contact.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01896" index="1896">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An item to be held by a Pokémon.\nThis cloak conceals the holder, protecting\nit from the additional effects of moves.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01897" index="1897">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An item to be held by a Pokémon.\nThis dice always rolls a good number,\nensuring multistrike moves hit more times.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01898" index="1898">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">N/A</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01899" index="1899">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A long loaf sliced\ninto top and bottom\nhalves.\rIts aroma of wheat and its straightforward,\nsalty flavor make it pair well with all\nkinds of sandwich ingredients.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01900" index="1900">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A condiment that packs a very tart\npunch yet pairs well with various\ningredients.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01901" index="1901">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A condiment with\nvery salty and\ntart flavor.\rWhile a number of other ingredients\ngo into its signature flavor, the\nnoble tomato is its heart and soul.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01902" index="1902">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very spicy condiment that’s indispensable\nwhen bread is on the table.\nIt pairs tremendously with ketchup.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01903" index="1903">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A condiment that unites salty and\nsweet and also packs a richness\nthat makes bread a delight to eat.\rThe finest butter products are\nmade of 100 percent Moomoo Milk.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01904" index="1904">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very sweet condiment.\nPeople in Paldea seem to favor the\nsweet varieties over the unsweetened.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01905" index="1905">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A condiment with a very spicy kick.\nIt’s thanks to Scovillain that this sauce\ngets its signature mouth-tingling burn.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01906" index="1906">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very salty\nseasoning,\nunsurprisingly.\rPeople quite like the grains of salt that\ncan be gathered from the footprints of\nparticularly jagged Naclstack.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01907" index="1907">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A seasoning\npacking very\nspicy flavor.\rIt goes nicely with oilier foods and works\nespecially well when you add just a pinch\nfor a hint of flavor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01908" index="1908">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A condiment that’s very sweet and very sour.\nIt goes especially well with fruit and\nis easy to incorporate into a sandwich.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01909" index="1909">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very sweet condiment.\nFolks in Paldea seem to love the varieties\nthat really let the sweetness sing.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01910" index="1910">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A condiment offering\nvery sweet and very\ntart flavor.\rIt goes well with more ingredients\nthan you’d expect, making it a\nconvenient go-to.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01911" index="1911">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A condiment that’s very\nsweet and likewise very\nsour.\rTake care when adding it to sandwiches,\nas the sweet side can overwhelm.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01912" index="1912">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A condiment with sour and bitter notes.\nIt’s surprisingly useful, as it makes\na nice counterpoint to oilier foods.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01913" index="1913">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A condiment offering\nfaint notes of sour\nand bitter flavors.\rThe most prized varieties are the ones\nSmoliv love the smell of--such oils’\nquality is assured.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01914" index="1914">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very sour condiment.\nVinegars derived from grapes\nare popular in Paldea.\rHighly effective when used to\nadd just a light note of flavor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01915" index="1915">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A legendary condiment\ntold of only in\nbooks.\rWord has it that one taste of its sweet\nflavor stimulates the digestive system and\ncures a lack of appetite.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01916" index="1916">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">One of the condiments\nspoken of as\nlegends.\rIts mellow saltiness is said to be\ntremendously effective when it comes to\npromoting health.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01917" index="1917">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This surpassingly sour condiment is\nsaid to be super effective in helping\nthe eater recover from exhaustion.\rOnly a scant few people know it exists.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01918" index="1918">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A legendary condiment\nwith a deeply bitter\ntaste.\rIt’s said to dramatically bolster a body’s\nimmune defenses, though that hasn’t\nbeen proven.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01919" index="1919">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">The legendary condiment\nsaid to have the mightiest\nof all spicy flavors.\rIt’s said that a single bite\nwill kick the metabolism\ninto high gear immediately.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01920" index="1920">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This bitter-tasting ingredient is simple\nand straightforward--just add it to all\nkinds of other ingredients for a\rdelightfully crunchy time.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01921" index="1921">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This very tart ingredient has a lot\nof savory elements to it, making it\npopular with many Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01922" index="1922">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very tart ingredient. Some varieties\nare also very sweet, and these are prized\nabove all others by the people of Paldea.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01923" index="1923">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A tart and bitter ingredient.\nUsing it together with rich-tasting\ningredients in a sandwich will really\rmake the most of a cucumber’s fresh-veggie\naroma.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01924" index="1924">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This very sour ingredient is made by\npickling veggies in a flavorful\nbrine made from spices and vinegar.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01925" index="1925">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This spicy veggie is indispensable\nto many sandwiches. It goes well\nwith rich ingredients.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01926" index="1926">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An ingredient with\nsome sweetness to\nit.\rIts spiciness and fragrance are milder\nthan those of other onions, making it\na pleasant bite.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01927" index="1927">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An ingredient with some bitterness.\nWhen sliced, it adds a nice accent\nto a sandwich.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01928" index="1928">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An ingredient with some bitterness--but\nits bitter notes and overall flavor are\npleasantly mild compared to its green\rcousin.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01929" index="1929">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An ingredient with some bitterness.\nIt’s not much different from its red\ncounterpart in flavor, but mixing\rthe colors makes a feast for the\neyes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01930" index="1930">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An ingredient with sweet notes--though its\nflavor is very mild. The avocado’s richness,\nhowever, makes it satisfying to eat.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01931" index="1931">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This very salty ingredient has been\ncooked just shy of charred, making it\nburst with fragrance and tasty flavor.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01932" index="1932">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very salty ingredient-and that\nvery saltiness is what makes it such\na nice companion to veggies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01933" index="1933">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This ingredient is very salty like regular\nham, but the difference is prosciutto is\nnot cooked after it is cured, giving it a\rfun freshness.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01934" index="1934">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very salty and spicy ingredient.\nThis type of sausage has\nparticularly robust salty flavor,\rand the spicier varieties are extra\npopular.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01935" index="1935">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very salty and bitter ingredient.\nThe balance between the potent\nsaltiness and the herbs’ bitterness\rmake this sausage a pleasure.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01936" index="1936">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This very salty ingredient is the\nthing to add if you want to make\nyour sandwich truly filling.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01937" index="1937">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very sweet and salty ingredient.\nIt’s a nutritious processed food made with a\nconcentrate derived from shed Klawf shells.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01938" index="1938">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very salty and bitter ingredient with\nthat unmistakable smoky flavor.\nIt pairs exceptionally well with veggies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01939" index="1939">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When used in a sandwich, this very salty\nand bitter ingredient is at its best paired\nwith sour seasonings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01940" index="1940">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An ingredient with a touch of saltiness.\nIt’s full of nutrients and can be enjoyed\nwith all sorts of seasonings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01941" index="1941">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very salty ingredient and\na popular dish in Paldea.\nIt’s undeniably filling.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01942" index="1942">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An ingredient with a touch of sweetness.\nIt’s unclear how well this raw block of\ntofu will serve as a sandwich filling.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01943" index="1943">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">An ingredient with a touch of sweetness.\nIt’s unclear how well this cooked rice\nwill serve as a sandwich filling.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01944" index="1944">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A nice salty ingredient.\nIt’s unclear how well these boiled noodles\nwill serve as a sandwich filling.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01945" index="1945">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This very tart ingredient--a soft\nsalad that’s all about potatoes--pairs\ntremendously well with bread.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01946" index="1946">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very salty ingredient. This thinly\nsliced cheese is perfect for adding\nto a sandwich.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01947" index="1947">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very sweet ingredient. This go-to\nfruit is sweet and rich, and it’s\nbeloved by many Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01948" index="1948">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very tart and sweet ingredient,\npopular for its ability to make a\nsandwich visually striking.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01949" index="1949">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This very sweet ingredient is sliced\nthin to make it easy to add into a\nsandwich.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01950" index="1950">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very tart ingredient that has a\nlight touch of sweetness as well. It\ngoes well with rich ingredients.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01951" index="1951">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This very tart ingredient is a fruit\nof southern lands, and its color\nand texture are a thrill.\rIt’s been cut into chunks to be easily\nmanageable.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01952" index="1952">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very spicy ingredient-so spicy as to\nleave no room for ambivalence about it.\nYou either like it or you don’t.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01953" index="1953">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very spicy condiment.\nIts distinctive sharp sizzle in your sinuses\nmakes it a good match for rich fillings.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01954" index="1954">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very spicy condiment. Just watch out--use\ntoo much of this potent seasoning, and it’ll\ncancel out the other flavors.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01955" index="1955">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">This very spicy condiment seems close\nto horseradish at first, but you’ll find\nthat it has a superb flavor all its own.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01956" index="1956">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very bitter ingredient that\nstands out among veggies for\nits quirky flavor.\rPeople tend to either like it or\nnot like it--they rarely sit on\nthe fence.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01957" index="1957">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A very bitter ingredient that’s quite\nversatile, as herbs go.\nIt’s fragrant and goes well with tomatoes.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_01958" index="1958">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">N/A</language>
	</row>
