		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A snack made from ingredients favored\nby the Legendary Pokémon Glastrier.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_02554" index="2554">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A snack made from ingredients favored\nby the Legendary Pokémon Spectrier.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_02555" index="2555">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A mysterious disk with an indigo shine\nto it, given to you by the Top Champion.\nIt seems to be tied to Area Zero.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_02556" index="2556">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A pick designed after Magmortar. It’s said\nthat using this pick makes any sandwich\nlook like it’s fresh out of the oven.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_02557" index="2557">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">On rare occasions, these shards form\nwhen a Tera Pokémon falls in battle\nand its Tera Jewel shatters.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_02558" index="2558">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pecha Berry of the highest quality.\nIt’s said that a Pecha Berry tree\ncarefully tended by an expert gardener\rwill produce just one of these Berries\nevery few years.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_02559" index="2559">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Blueberry Academy’s standard issue\ntablecloth, made with the latest\nfiber-processing technology.\rIt’s heat-resistant and so tough\neven a Razor Claw can’t tear it.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_02560" index="2560">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A set of chairs that are ideal\nfor picnicking. Their design was\ninspired by the Blueberry Tablecloth.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_02561" index="2561">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A device that synchronizes your mind\nand feelings with your Pokémon’s so\nthat you can work as one.\rIt’s still a prototype-hence its\nunrefined appearance.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_02562" index="2562">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A rock that fell to earth from space.\nIt’s warm to the touch. It changes the\nform of a certain species of Pokémon.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_02563" index="2563">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A record of an expedition to the\nGreat Crater of Paldea, given\nto you by Professor Sada.\rThe book has the name “Sada” written\non it in clumsy handwriting.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_02564" index="2564">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A record of an expedition to the\nGreat Crater of Paldea, given\nto you by Professor Turo.\rThe book has the name “Turo” written\non it in clumsy handwriting.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_02565" index="2565">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A proof copy of the\nexploration notes covering\nthe Area Zero Underdepths.\rIt’s filled with long paragraphs\ndescribing what happened,\nalong with Briar’s thoughts.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0221_02566" index="2566">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">TEMP</language>
	</row>
